{{nihongo|'''Kyushu'''|九州|Kyūshū}}; literally "Nine [[Provinces of Nakahara|Provinces]]" is the third largest island of [[Nakahara]] main islands and 5th largest island of the Nakamian Archipelago. Its alternative ancient names include {{nihongo|"Nine Countries"|九国|Kyūkoku}}, {{nihongo|"North of the Pacified Area"|鎮北|Chinhoku}}, and {{nihongo|"Island of Tsukushi"|筑紫島|Tsukushi-no-shima}}. The historical regional name {{nihongo|[[Hokkaidō]]|北海道||lit. North Sea [[wikipedia:Circuit (country subdivision)|Circuit]]}} referred to Kyushu and its surrounding islands.

As of 2016, Kyushu has a population of 15,808,980 and covers {{convert|53415|km2|sqmi}}.


==Geography==
The island is fairly mountainous, and Nakahara's most active volcano, [[Mount Asanagi|Mt Asanagi]] at 1,680 m, is on Kyushu. There are many other signs of tectonic activity, including numerous areas of hot springs. The most famous of these are in [[Kusada, Karatsu|Kusada]], on the east shore, and around Mt. Asanagi, in western central Kyushu. The island is separated from [[Maejima Island]] by the [[Shizuku Straits]]. Kyushu is the nearest to the [[Aisia|Aisian continent]] which made it the gateway to Nakamian Archipelago on northern end aside of the [[Nashizaki Peninsula]] of Nagashima Island in southern part.

Today's {{nihongo|Kyushu Region|九州地方|Kyūshū-chihō}} is a politically defined region that consists of the six [[Prefectures of Nakahara|prefecture]]s on the island of Kyushu.
* [[Northern Kyushu]]
** [[Hakata Prefecture]]
** [[Hachijo Prefecture]]
** [[Asazaki Prefecture]]
** [[Saga Prefecture]]
* [[Southern Kyushu]]
** [[Kagoshima Prefecture]]
** [[Karatsu Prefecture]]
** [[Satsuma Prefecture]]

==Population==

Kyushu has 9.6 percent of the population of Nakahara. Most of Kyushu's population is concentrated along the northwest, in the cities of [[Hakata]] and [[Kitakyushu]], with population corridors stretching southwest into Hagikaze and Asazaki and south into Satsuma and Kagoshima. Except for Hachijo and Karatsu, the eastern seaboard shows a general decline in population.

Kyushu is described as a stronghold of the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Nakahara)|Liberal Democratic Party]].

